john constantine has a long history  across every version of dc's expansive  universe but what are his true origins  and was he actually the reason swamp  thing was able to have a daughter stay  tuned to find out  before we get into the in-universe  history of dc's unluckiest mystic it's  worth taking a look at the  behind-the-scenes story of how he came  to be  after all while most of the uk's famous  fictional spellcasters descend from the  tradition of merlin our boy john was  inspired by a very different british  hero gordon sumner better known to the  world as sting the story behind john  constantine's first appearance in 1985's  swamp thing number 37 is pretty simple  when writer alan moore asked artists  steven bessette and john totalben what  they'd like to draw they told him they  wanted to draw sting or at least someone  who looked like him  moore thought sting's striking look  would work for the charismatic  manipulative magician that he had in  mind and thus john constantine stepped  onto the page as for the specific visual  references that bessette and total ben  were drawing from the long coat and suit  look that would become john  constantine's trademark was inspired by  sting's appearance in 1979's  quadrophenia based on the who album of  the same name another inspiration though  was much more esoteric a 1982 tv movie  called brimstone and tree cull where  sting played a disturbing fourth wall  breaking character who may or may not  have been the devil pretty fitting all  things considered saying that john  constantine has had a rough life is  putting things mildly there are very few  characters in comics who've had quite as  much misery heaped on them over the  years in john's case as revealed in  hellblazer number 39 it started even  before he was born as a child jon  occasionally had visions of what he  called the golden boy he was essentially  just that an imaginary friend made up of  shining golden light that john both  loved and hated for his seeming  perfection  after he grew up though jon learned that  he was neither imaginary nor a friend  but a parallel world echo of the twin  brother he never knew he had the  existence of a twin wasn't just news to  him the doctors who delivered jon as a  baby were also pretty surprised when it  turned out that mary ann constantine had  been pregnant with a second child the  other brother was so sickly and  underweight that he'd gone unnoticed  unfortunately he had been strangled in  the womb and neither he nor mary  survived the birth the surviving infant  of course was john  his childhood was marked by intense  hatred and resentment from his father  who made it very clear that he wished  john had been the one who died instead  john and his father thomas constantine  didn't get along while john was growing  up  not only did thomas blame jon for mary's  death but he was also disappointed in  him for other reasons tom wanted a  normal son who would fit in with the  other kids at school rather than a young  weirdo who spent all his time on books  about magic and demons  the elder constantine burned a stack of  his son's books and a fit of anger  hoping to drive him away from sorcery  this might have worked out for the best  but jon was furious he decided to get  back at his dad so he cursed him by  binding his soul to a dead cat  before long thomas was wasting away from  an inexplicable disease as the feline  corpse rotted but jon was left feeling  guilty about what he'd done to his old  man  since the spell couldn't be reversed he  preserved the cat in formaldehyde  stopping his father from degenerating  any further cut to a few decades later  and thomas finally died only for his  soul to be stuck on earth he terrified  john's niece gemma until jon realized  that as long as the preserved cat was  around thomas would be bound by it and  would continue suffering to free him jon  dug up the cat from under his mother's  tombstone where he buried it he then  burned the corpse finally setting his  father free if john constantine has an  origin story in the traditional  superhero sense then it's what went down  with the newcastle crew's disastrous  attempt to help a young girl the gory  details are in hellblazer number 11 and  they are not for the faint of heart it  happens early on in john's career as a  freelance magician when he hears about  some bad stuff going down at the  casanova club the club's owner was  involved with the same sort of shady  magic scene as jon but his proclivities  were far more disturbing including the  abuse of his daughter astra logue  eventually astra manifested a monster  called norfolk thing and after being  summoned the norfolk thing does to the  club owner and his guests exactly what  they did to astra it also tore off their  heads and turned the basement of the  casanova into a carnal house to deal  with the norfolk thing jon gathered six  other occultists to form the newcastle  crew from there he came up with the  not-so-brilliant plan of summoning a  powerful demon to kill astra's monster  but when john found out what was  happening with the girl  he decided  was gonna  it did not go well while the ritual was  correct constantine got the wrong name  for the demon since the name is the  thing that provided the control he  essentially unleashed a horrifying and  hungry force on himself his friends and  poor astra the demon nergal did destroy  the norfolk thing but it then turned on  jon and his friends jon was forced to  lead astra through hell itself in an  attempt to save her soul and while he  held tight to her hand for the whole  trip said hand didn't stay attached to  the rest of the girl she was dragged to  hell and the rest of the newcastle crew  was left traumatized they all met grisly  fates before their souls were condemned  to hell as for jon he managed to avoid  eternal damnation but he wound up  suffering his own personal health for  the next few years the contingency plan  for summoning the demon at the casanova  was one that we can probably all get  behind blowing it up with a very  enthusiastic round of arson  unfortunately for jon setting things on  fire tends to be very effective at both  solving problems and creating them when  this bizarre magician emerged from a  fire clutching a severed hand and  ranting about a demon that dragged him  to hell he wound up being taken to the  raven scar secure hospital a miserable  and disreputable asylum for the  criminally insane the chief problem for  constantine was that while he was  certainly traumatized he wasn't  hallucinating there was a demon that was  after his soul but the only thing that  the staff and inmates of ravensgaard  knew was that all this bad stuff  happened and jon was involved as a  result constantine was beaten by the  inmates and tortured by the doctors  under the guise of treatment with  electro-convulsive therapy being a  favorite tactic all of this only served  to amplify his self-loathing and the  guilt he felt for his plan going so  horrifically wrong as hellblazer number  50 put it in one of its typically  cheerful moments the only reason he  hated them was that they wouldn't cut  his throat and end the agony john's  tenure at ravenscar lasted two years but  the memory of both the events that led  him there and the treatment he received  in its walls would haunt him for the  rest of his life  like a lot of comic book characters  there are different versions of john  constantine's backstory depending on  what comics you're reading but his path  is weirder than most when he was  introduced in the pages of swamp thing  it was as part of the dc universe most  of his series however was published by  dc's vertigo imprint a line initially  focused on horror titles for adult  readers that was separated from the  bright super-heroic world of the main dc  comics  eventually after 20 years of being  sequestered in his own supernatural  universe constantine was folded back  into the dcu proper his origin was then  revised with a little less of the  disturbing darkness involved the new  origin story that led constantine to  join the justice league dark and deal  with the dc universe's magical threats  still wound its way through newcastle  astrolog's damnation and a stint in  ravenscar asylum this time though things  started to go bad much earlier in  constantine number 14 readers learned  that at a very young age john  encountered some sinister demonic force  that offered him magical power jon  eagerly accepted but as is usually the  case with this sort of thing he wasn't  told about the price of this power until  it was too late to do anything about it  the price in typically tragic fashion  was jon's home and family in his first  use of magic constantine burnt down his  childhood house standing untouched in  the center of the flames while his  mother and father were burned to death  in front of him there is one element of  constantine's pre-trench coat life  that's consistent among various versions  of the character before he started  skulking around in his iconic duster  manipulating swamp monsters into doing  his mysterious and vaguely sinister  bidding he was into some really  disreputable stuff rock and roll in his  younger days constantine under the not  so great stage name johnny conjob was  the lead singer in a punk band called  mucus membrane  according to constantine himself they  weren't very good when it came to the  actual music but their brief time in the  grotesque spotlights of british punk  clubs did see them find some success  of course that had a lot less to do with  their musical talent than it did with  the undeniable charisma of their front  man the reason that mucous membrane  broke up varies from one series to the  next in the current dc universe it was  prompted by constantine's use of magic  as part of his stagecraft it caused his  bandmate and lover veronica delacroix to  fade away from the physical world until  she became a disembodied spirit  in the classic vertigo comics it had  more to do with the newcastle incident  and john's subsequent commitment to  ravenskar at one point an amateur  documentary crew trying to find out what  happened to mucous membrane starred in a  story that ran through hellblazer number  245 to 246.  in this arc they were all violently  murdered by the remnants of asterisk  terror elemental the norfolk thing  another one of the more consistent  elements in constantine's life is his  romantic history with stage magician  legitimate sorceress and justice leaguer  zatana zatara  the backward talking spellcaster  predates jon's portrayal in comics by 20  years but their pasts have been depicted  as being intertwined since very early in  constantine's existence  see you all right  yeah as soon as you get off me  i should have known you were the reason  i'm not back in london enjoying a pint  sadly the way their lives are tangled  together is about as tragic as  everything else in constantine's past  while they do maintain some level of  affection for each other there is a  pretty big sticking point in their  history that prompted their initial  breakup constantine killed her dad  he didn't intentionally end john  zatara's life but he was the driving  force behind the magic ritual that  resulted in her father bursting into  flames and dying in front of them in the  original comics this was an attempt to  deal with the mystical side of the  multiverse shattering event seen in  crisis on infinite earths but a similar  event exists even in the current  continuity where the crisis didn't  happen before they broke up zatana cast  a spell on jon telling him you need to  be a better person though of course she  said it in her backward way of  spellcasting that would explain why  constantine is less of a loner and a bit  more eager to help these days wouldn't  it  constantine was originally introduced as  a supporting character for swamp thing  and while he's had plenty of success on  his own he's always had that association  there's another reason that those  characters will always be inextricably  linked though believe it or not the saga  of swamp thing is at its heart a romance  between the eponymous muk monster and  his wife abby arcane at one point after  the creation of a seed that would  combine swampy's plant-based essence  with a human soul abby and the swamp  thing decided to have a child of their  own the problem was that swamp thing was  not human and didn't have the right  equipment for the job what he did have  was the ability to take over someone  else's body using semi-mystical plant  spores and a person who owed him several  favors with that in mind swamp thing  took over john constantine's body flew  to louisiana and then used him to  impregnate abby with their daughter to  faye  after constantine manipulated him into  several dubious semi-sinister errands of  his own swamp thing felt justified in  his actions as a means to an end  the tree that swamp thing got tattooed  on constantine's rear end while he was  piloting the guy's body however was pure  revenge check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite comics are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you

